{# The admin bar as the public site draws it for a signed-in user (TASK-183),
   put straight after the theme's <body> tag.

   Whatever theme the site wears has never heard of it, so it keeps to a shadow
   root: no selector of the theme's reaches the markup inside, and the
   stylesheet inside reaches nothing outside. The stylesheet is inlined rather
   than linked so the bar is never drawn unstyled; the public site has no
   content CSP to refuse it.

   The host is fixed to the top of the window, as WordPress's is. In normal
   flow it sat inside whatever padding or margin the theme gave <body>, so it
   stopped short of the window's edges. Out of flow, nothing the theme does to
   <body> moves it, and the inline reset keeps the theme's rules for the host
   element itself, a `body > *` or a grid on <body>, from restyling it; only an
   `!important` rule can, which is also how a theme that insists hides it. The
   page is pushed down from outside, by a stylesheet the CMS puts in <head>
   (OFFSET_STYLE in src/web/admin-bar.ts) reading --geekity-admin-bar-height.

   The script does two things. It measures the bar and sets that height on
   <html>, so a bar that wraps to two lines on a phone, or one a theme has
   hidden, pushes the page down by what it really is. And it gives focus back
   to the greeting when the menu closes with focus inside it: Chrome does that
   for a popover in the light DOM, not from inside a shadow root, where the
   focus is simply lost. A click elsewhere has already moved focus by then,
   and keeps it. #}
<geekity-admin-bar style="all: initial; display: block; position: fixed; top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; z-index: 99999"><template shadowrootmode="open"><style>{% include "static/admin-bar.css" %}</style>{% include "components/admin-bar.njk" %}<script>
(() => {
  const host = document.querySelector('geekity-admin-bar');
  const root = host.shadowRoot;
  new ResizeObserver(() => {
    const height = host.getBoundingClientRect().height;
    document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--geekity-admin-bar-height', `${height}px`);
  }).observe(host);
  const menu = root.getElementById('admin-account-menu');
  menu?.addEventListener('beforetoggle', (event) => {
    if (event.newState === 'closed' && menu.contains(root.activeElement)) {
      setTimeout(() => root.querySelector('.admin-bar-account').focus());
    }
  });
})();
</script></template></geekity-admin-bar>
